/// How many lines a session keeps before the oldest is dropped. A terminal
/// scrollback holds far more, so a session that outgrows this has already lost
/// anything the user would go looking for.
const HISTORY_LIMIT: usize = 1000;

/// The most binding changes `.undo` can walk back.
///
/// A step holds a copy of the session's bindings, so an unbounded stack is a
/// copy of the session per keystroke. Fifty is far more than a user retries by
/// hand and small enough that the copies cannot grow without bound; past it the
/// oldest step is dropped and the session says so rather than quietly keeping a
/// shorter history than it promised.
const MAX_UNDO: usize = 50;

/// The most named checkpoints one session may hold, for the same reason.
const MAX_CHECKPOINTS: usize = 64;

/// The most lines a block may hold before the session stops waiting for its
/// `end`.
///
/// Nobody types five hundred lines into one block by accident, and a piped block
/// that is never closed — `printf 'repeat 3 times\n' | rb`, or a generator that
/// forgot its `end` — buffered without limit until the process ran out of memory.
/// Past this the session says the block is incomplete and starts over, which is
/// what the user would have to do by hand anyway.
const MAX_BLOCK_LINES: usize = 500;

/// The most bytes a block may hold, for the same reason and for the same inputs:
/// a block of a few very long lines gets nowhere near [`MAX_BLOCK_LINES`] and can
/// still be enormous.
const MAX_BLOCK_BYTES: usize = 64 * 1024;

/// How many lines of an unclosed block are echoed back when the session ends or
/// gives up. The rest are counted and reported, so the report itself cannot be
/// the thing that floods a terminal.
const BLOCK_REPORT_LINES: usize = 20;

/// How many names a `.edit` will try for its own directory under the temporary
/// one, before it reports that it could not have one.
///
/// One is the number that would be right if nobody else were sharing the
#[derive(Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ReplCommand {
    /// A line that is Redblue source rather than a command.
    ///
    /// This is not [`ReplCommand::Unknown`]: `say "hi"` is not a mistyped
    /// command, it is a program. Conflating the two made the REPL answer
    /// `2 + 3` with "Unknown command '2 + 3'" and refuse to evaluate it.
    NotACommand,
    Quit,
    Help,
    Clear,
    History,
    Vars,
    Functions,
    /// Runs a shell command in the host shell and reports its output and exit.
    ///
    /// The command text is kept whole rather than split into words: the shell
    /// is the parser for it, and `!echo a | wc -l` is one command with its own
    /// pipeline in it.
    Shell(String),
    /// Sends the session's last result to a shell command's standard input.
    Pipe(String),
    /// Moves the session's working directory, which every relative file
    /// argument is resolved against.
    ChangeDir(String),
    /// Prints the session's working directory.
    PrintWorkingDirectory,
    /// Lists the session's working directory.
    ListDirectory,
    Load(String),
    Save(String),
    /// Reads a history file written by [`ReplCommand::Save`] back into the
    /// session's history.
    ///
    /// The other half of `:save`, which had no half: a saved file could not be
